{"id": "EUVD-2026-93136", "enisaUuid": "5ccc4a2d-2caa-351a-82ef-148865f93a70", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nmmc: sdio_uart: fix xmit_fifo leak when the port table is full\n\nsdio_uart_add_port() allocates the transmit fifo before claiming a\nslot in sdio_uart_table[].  When all UART_NR slots are taken, it\nreturns -EBUSY with the fifo still allocated, but the probe error\npath only kfree()s the port, leaking the transmit fifo.\n\nFree the fifo in the failure path of sdio_uart_add_port() itself so\nthe function retains nothing on error.", "datePublished": "2026-10-06T08:44:45", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:15:39", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/9e992d59138fcfaa4bad7cc0750265b0a8bca100", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/b97b5b66c93cb4aaf6358727a73fff880a774dfd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/8a2c1bf209ba04cbd14153a771724bd5aa522fcd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/72f4c2b7a48423c708f2c348585419a1b71ab04c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fd8223c53ad9553b2a349d2a40e19bbc6e60fc48", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/ac866db277a4c73e84b4263773652e3aba326249", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/5e142adbbdc54afbd01fad476c91cded41d22594", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/53823e25793a97d07e6e98e0904bbf74cac8bc76"], "aliases": ["GHSA-4c3r-52hj-39rr", "CVE-2026-98208"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.18, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0ae31a2c-9e25-37b3-b180-71ac37ab64f0", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8b197a5ce7a7218bb9fc721647ba0d5734f27348 <9e992d59138fcfaa4bad7cc0750265b0a8bca100"}, {"id": "0e37484a-b63c-3148-9269-4b5ab4e13b1e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "8b197a5ce7a7218bb9fc721647ba0d5734f27348 <72f4c2b7a48423c708f2c348585419a1b71ab04c"}, {"id": "306d5e1c-66c9-3cc4-a23c-6b80f9bc0c4e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id":